    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d788">

                <pb facs="0878" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg786"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.7311/12</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-22T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3696. My 2987, January 3, 11 a.m., and previous telegrams.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d788-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affairs of Montenegro has just
                    informed me that the King proposes to name as envoy extraordinary and minister
                        <pb facs="0879" n="787" xml:id="pg787"/> plenipotentiary to United States,
                    General Doctor Antoine Gvosdenovitch,
                    aide-de-camp to the King, and would be glad to know if this person would be <hi
                        rendition="#italic">persona grata</hi> to the Federal Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
